  "description": {
    "text": "Demonstration copies of Expedition's Pichu and Hoppip for the e-Reader kiosks Nintendo sent to video game shops across North America when the e-Reader and Expedition came out in September 2002. The two cards and an e-Reader \"Manhole\" card hung from each kiosk on a metal cable threaded through a hole punched in each card, so customers could swipe them through the e-Reader without help; together Pichu and Hoppip unlock its game Hold Down Hoppip. Apart from the coating and the hole they are the ordinary non-holo Expedition prints, with the English back.\n\nA further set of three went out for staff lanyards, so staff could step in if the kiosk cards were damaged. The copies come in two finishes, a thick gloss on front and back, and a thin gloss on the front with a matte back; collectors guess the fully glossy set was the one on the kiosks, which would make the matte-backed one the lanyard set. They turn up for sale fairly often.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "pichu.blog: The 8 identical-artwork Pichu cards from Expedition",
        "url": "https://pichu.blog/english-expedition-base-set"
      },
